        ":question/problem": "The inequality $-5\\le x<-2$ can be expressed in interval notation as",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Every inequality can be expressed as an interval. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ if the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nFor the given inequality \n\n$$\n-5\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,x\\,\\,<\\,\\,-2\n$$\n\nwe note the following:\n\n- The left endpoint $-5$ *is* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $[\\,.$\n\n- The right endpoint $-2$ is *not* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $)\\,.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding interval is\n\n$$\nx\\in [-5,-2).\n$$",
